{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:be7859b46b3b9cd5","name":"TT-8L Gatekeeper Droid","source":{"id":"source:reference-be7859b46b3b9cd5","title":"TT-8L Gatekeeper Droid","revision":21123,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T01:12:08Z","sha256":"5dc3960955ce01e373b72f25ee0edc2d07459ef3f1eb73db120f8da623dca4b6","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=21123","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=TT-8L%20Gatekeeper%20Droid&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-be7859b46b3b9cd5","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scavenger's Guide to Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scavenger%27s_Guide_to_Droids"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The TT-8L Gatekeeper Droid is Serv-O-Droid's answer to the door guard. The unit is not much more than a large, spherical eye attached to the end of a long, snakelike body that maneuvers with support from its permanent base. The Droid has audio sensors and a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vocabulator"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vocabulator","referenceId":"reference:a28880d579fbd223"}," that allows it to interact with whomever attempts to enter the facility where it watches the door.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Ever since its creation around the time of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi Civil War"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi_Civil_War"},", the TT-8L has worked with a simple purpose: Let only authorized personnel pass. However, the designers made the Droid too good at its job. The TT-8L adheres so closely to the letter of its programming that last-minute additions to a list are often forced to wait until they can be confirmed by a member of the staff. In fact, the vast majority of Gatekeeper Droids develop highly annoying personalities that grate on the nerves of those forced to wait for permission to pass.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["TT-8L Gatekeeper Droids can't be played as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Heroes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Heroes"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["More Trouble Than it’s Worth"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Working with TT-8L Gatekeeper Droids can be frustrating at best. They tend to ask questions of every single sentient being that wants to walk through your front door. It does not matter whether the being in question has been previously approved, whether the being is accompanied by someone who has been cleared to pass, or whether the being was inside already, had to step out for something, and now wants to be readmitted. Worse, TT-8Ls insist on reporting every single question and answer exchanged with every single being they stop. That in itself is enough to create trouble on a grand scale, if the Droid happens to stop the wrong visitor."]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["I seem to recall hearing that a Gatekeeper blew a circuit not long ago. It was standing guard at the entrance to a recently abandoned facility in the mountains of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Cularin"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Cularin"},". A recovery expedition arrived to clear out the rest of the facility before its supplies could be taken by pirates or looters. The team entered the place easily enough, but the TT-8L sealed the hatch and would not let them out. When they tried to approach the Droid to shut it down and open the door, the Gatekeeper summoned Battle Droids that were left behind to protect it. I imagine that those trapped people are probably running out of food and supplies about now and in dire need of rescue."]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["-",{"tag":"a","children":["EV-6T6"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/EV-6T6?action=edit&redlink=1"}]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Encountering a TT-8L Gatekeeper Droid"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["TT-8L Gatekeeper Droids are almost always found at doors, gates, or other entryways where the occupants of the area beyond require a sentry to monitor access. For example, the heroes might be standing outside the main entrance to the headquarters of a band of mercenaries on a remote Outer Rim world. A TT-8L Droid pokes its eye through a small window in the gate to see who requests entrance and to determine whether the visitor is legitimate.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Meanwhile, four to eight guards in a 3x3-square room connected to the foyer on the other side of the gate wait for a signal from the Droid. If the TT-8L denies the heroes passage and they try to force their way through, the guards spring into action and take defensive positions around the gate.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Modification: Advance Scout Droid"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Since TT-8L Gatekeeper Droids are stationary for most of their period of service, they eagerly accept modifications that allow them to move around. Still, turning a Gatekeeper Droid into an advance scout requires some drastic adjustments. The first step is to choose a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"},"- typically, something light and fast, such as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Speeder Bike"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Speeder_Bike"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Once the mode of transportation has been selected, prepare the Droid's skill set to operate the Vehicle. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reprogram"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reprogram"}," its ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knowledge (Bureaucracy)"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knowledge_(Bureaucracy)"}," skill to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pilot","referenceId":"reference:383e2d946278a872"},", which will automatically change the corresponding ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skill Training"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skill_Training","referenceId":"reference:fa24e9bf050e743e"}," feat. Optionally, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reprogram"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reprogram"}," the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skill Focus (Persuasion)"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skill_Focus_(Persuasion)"}," feat to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pilot","referenceId":"reference:383e2d946278a872"}," as well. Remove the Droid from its base and implant it into the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"},". With a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Speeder Bike"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Speeder_Bike"},", the appendage is clamped down along the top of the fuselage, and the primary section of the Droid that includes its brain is secured near the rear of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Modification: Communications Antenna"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["This particular modification works in emergency situations where a communications array has been damaged or destroyed. By setting up the proper equipment ahead of time as modules, the equipment can be attached to the TT-8L without making permanent changes to the Droid. To begin, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reprogram"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reprogram"}," one of the Droid's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skills"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skills","referenceId":"reference:66d0f523a379b2de"},", such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Persuasion"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Persuasion","referenceId":"reference:196fbdc5f1823320"},", to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"},", and shift the corresponding ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skill Focus"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skill_Focus","referenceId":"reference:453339c8a3cf4f4c"}," feat to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," as well.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Next, install an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Internal Comlink"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Internal_Comlink","referenceId":"reference:7fadfdfea7aba7e9"}," (Long-Range) or a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hypertransceiver"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hypertransceiver"}," into an attachable pod, depending on the range you want to establish. Adding the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hypertransceiver"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hypertransceiver"}," requires a DC 30 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," check and 2 days of work. Wiring the TT-8L's appendage to function as an antenna is a simple procedure that requires a DC 15 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," check and 10 minutes of work. Once modifications are complete, attaching the communications module to the Droid takes a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Full-Round Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Full-Round_Action"},", and removing it takes a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swift Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swift_Action"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Modification: Security Camera"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Using the TT-8L Gatekeeper Droid as a security camera accomplishes virtually the same goal as the primary objective for the Droid, but the responsibility of granting entrance to authorized visitors is shifted to the Droid's master or another designated individual. The advantage of using a TT-8L instead of a passive security camera is that the Droid is capable of judging whether the information it gathers about the visitors is important to the decision maker.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["To make this modification, start by adding either a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Video Recorder"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Video_Recorder"}," or a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Holo Recorder"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Holo_Recorder"}," to the Droid, and tie the Recording Unit's reception through the Droid's photoreceptor. Next, remove the TT-8L from its base and mount it at the desired location- perhaps a strategic intersection of corridors or within a hidden recess high on a wall. Once the Droid is in place, either wire it to the facility's security camera system or computer network, or configure it to transmit data wirelessly to whoever needs to view the information.\n"]},"\n","\n\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["TT-8L Gatekeeper Droid Statistics (CL 0)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n","Large ",{"tag":"a","children":["3rd-Degree Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/3rd-Degree_Droid"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 1\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," -3; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Darkvision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darkvision"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +14\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Binary"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Binary","referenceId":"reference:ee1c8277caf5fb9b"},", 3 Unassigned\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 6 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 6), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"hr